110.docs:
A [`Chat`] that answers from the films of a [`MovieLibrary`]. It looks only at
the words the films hold, on this machine, with no model.

The messages are the app's, so that they outlive a closed panel, and `on_open`
says what opening a moment means there, usually going to the film with a
[`MovieCue`](crate::MovieCue).

```
use ravenrs_movie::{MovieChat, MovieLibrary};
use ravenrs_reactive::State;
use ravenrs_widgets::ChatMessage;

let messages = State::new(Vec::<ChatMessage>::new());
let chat = MovieChat::new(MovieLibrary::new(), messages.binding(), |moment| {
    println!("open {}", moment.title);
});
```

864.docs:
Keeps the last warnings and errors logged with `tracing`, in memory only, to give
to [`BugReporter::errors`](crate::BugReporter::errors), where the person sees them
before anything goes. Add it to the app's subscriber as a layer.

```
use ravenrs_movie::RecentErrors;
use tracing_subscriber::layer::SubscriberExt as _;

let errors = RecentErrors::default();
let subscriber = tracing_subscriber::registry().with(errors.clone());
tracing::subscriber::with_default(subscriber, || tracing::error!(code = 7, "could not save"));
assert_eq!(errors.lines(), ["could not save code=7"]);
```

94.docs:
The films of an app, ready to be asked about. Cloning is cheap.

```
use ravenrs_core::{Color, Size};
use ravenrs_movie::{FilmBuilder, MovieLibrary};

let mut film = FilmBuilder::new(Size::new(320.0, 200.0), Color::WHITE);
film.frame(0, &[]);
film.chapter("Pagar uma conta", "Como dar baixa no que venceu.", 0);
let library = MovieLibrary::new().film("Manual", film.finish(1000)?);
assert_eq!(library.ask("como pago as contas?", 3)[0].moment.title, "Pagar uma conta");
# Ok::<(), ravenrs_movie::MovieError>(())
```
